SUMMARY:Toronto Workshop on Moral Psychology and Moral Theory
DESCRIPTION:The Toronto Workshop on Moral Psychology and Moral Theory is a forum for work at the intersection of empirical moral psychology and fundamental moral theory. The Workshop will take place on Saturday and Sunday\, November 7 and 8\, at the Jackman Humanities Building at the University of Toronto. All sessions will be entirely in person and will consist of 45-minute talks followed by 40-minute Q&A sessions. Any questions? E-mail the conference organizer\, Andrew Sepielli\, at torontomoralpsych@gmail.com. \nIt is free to attend the sessions. We ask only that you register by October 15 indicating your intention to attend. \n\nSpeakers: \n\n\nPaul Bloom (Psychology\, University of Toronto) \nJames Cornwell (Psychology\, Wheaton College) \nRyan Davis (Political Science\, Brigham Young University) \nBrendan de Kenessey (Philosophy\, University of Toronto) \nJoshua Knobe (Philosophy and Psychology\, Yale University) \nLarisa Heiphetz Solomon (Psychology\, Columbia University) \nRoseanna Sommers (Law\, University of Michigan) \nYuji Winet (Business\, Duke University) \nLiane Young (Psychology\, Boston University) \nMike Zhao (Philosophy\, University of Notre Dame)
URL:https://philosophy.utoronto.ca/event/toronto-workshop-on-moral-psychology-and-moral-theory/
LOCATION:Jackman Humanities Building 100
CATEGORIES:Graduate,St. George,UTM,UTSC
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://philosophy.utoronto.ca/wp-content/uploads/Moral-Psych-Conference-Poster-cropped.png
END:VEVENT
