UID:36056-1794571200-1794582000@philosophy.utoronto.ca
SUMMARY:CANCELLED - Continental Philosophy Research Group (Dimitris Vardoulakis\, Western Sydney University)
DESCRIPTION:This talk has unfortunately been cancelled. \nThe Continental Philosophy Research Interest Group is delighted to welcome as guest speaker Dimitris Vardoulakis\, who was the inaugural chair of Philosophy at Western Sydney University. Some of his books include Spinoza\, the Epicurean: Authority and Utility in Materialism (2020); The Ruse of Techne: Heidegger’s Magical Materialism (2024); The Agonistic Condition: Materialism and Democracy (2025); and The Logic of Living: The Materialism of Ancient Greek Thought (forthcoming). He is the co-editor of the book series “Incitements” (Edinburgh University Press) and the journal Philosophy\, Politics and Critique. He is currently Vice President of the Council of the Humanities\, Arts and Social Sciences (CHASS) and has served as chair of the Australasian Society for Continental Philosophy (ASCP). \nTitle\nWhat is Materialism? \nAbstract\nIf we reflect on the use of the word “materialism\,” we will be confounded by its diverse and even contradictory meanings: It can refer both to the “material girl” as the embodied subject of high capitalism and neoliberalism\, and to the historical materialist dialectic of Marx\, or Marxism. It describes both Spinoza’s equation of god and nature that leads to a radical politics\, and the naturalist principle that everything is subject to causality and hence scientifically understandable\, which seems to lack a politics altogether. \nIn this presentation\, I will argue that how we understand the history of materialism affects what we understand by this term. To present this position\, I will synthesize insights from four books on the history and politics of materialism that I have published since 2020. The upshot will be the argument that materialism is a much more powerful analytic concept in politics than it has been recognized hitherto.
URL:https://philosophy.utoronto.ca/event/continental-philosophy-research-group-dimitris-vardoulakis-western-sydney-university/
LOCATION:Factor-Inwentash Faculty of Social Work\, 246 Bloor Street West\, Room 620\, Toronto\, ON\, M5S 1V4\, Canada
CATEGORIES:Graduate,St. George
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://philosophy.utoronto.ca/wp-content/uploads/Dimitris-resized.png
END:VEVENT
